    "summary": "Cloth, a piece of imported cotton cloth, with a warp-faced pattern of alternating blue and white warp threads, divided by thin red lines (the edges have a different pattern). The weft is blue. This has been adapted by the Kalabari by cutting out sections of the white warp threads to create a repeating stepped pattern of diamond shapes (the process called ‘pelete bite’). See Af1981,11.1 for an uncut piece of the same pattern. The cloth has not been hemmed.",
